---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../../components/sections/LegalPage.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | WAMOCON GmbH" description="Privacy policy of WAMOCON GmbH for the website, contact inquiries and application inquiries." lang={lang}>
  <LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" updated="Last updated: 21 July 2026">
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>
      WAMOCON GmbH<br />
      Mergenthalerallee 79 - 81<br />
      65760 Eschborn, Germany<br />
      Phone: <a href="tel:+4961965838311">+49 6196 5838311</a><br />
      Email and privacy inquiries: <a href="mailto:info@wamocon.com">info@wamocon.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Managing Director: Dipl.-Ing. Waleri Moretz<br />
      Local Court Frankfurt am Main, HRB 103893<br />
      VAT identification number: DE303792072
    </p>
    <p>No Data Protection Officer has been appointed.</p>

    <h2>2. Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. Vercel processes technically necessary connection data such as
      IP address, time, requested URL, referrer, browser and operating system to provide the website securely
      and reliably under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. The regular availability of runtime logs depends on the Vercel
      plan and, according to Vercel's current documentation, is limited to no more than 30 days. Data affected
      by a specific security incident may be kept until the incident has been resolved. Our application does
      not write names, contact details or message text to its own logs. A data processing agreement is in place.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Contact and application inquiries</h2>
    <p>
      Our forms are exclusively for non-binding inquiries. We process your name, at least one contact channel
      chosen by you (email or phone), your message and any application information you provide. The legal
      bases are Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for pre-contractual steps and Article 6(1)(f) GDPR for other inquiries.
      Vercel and Microsoft 365/Microsoft Graph are used for transmission and internal notification under data
      processing agreements.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact inquiries are deleted no later than 24 months after completion unless legal retention duties or
      a subsequent contract require longer storage. Application data is deleted no later than six months
      after the application process ends. Longer inclusion in a talent pool requires separate voluntary consent.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Aptitude test for apprenticeships (Google Forms)</h2>
    <p>
      Our apprenticeship page offers a voluntary aptitude test. This test is not provided by us but through
      Google Forms, a service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. You
      leave our website and are forwarded to Google only when you actively click the aptitude-test button.
      Simply visiting our page transfers no data to Google.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you take part, Google processes the answers you enter as well as technical connection data,
      in particular your IP address, browser and device data. We receive the test results and the contact
      details you provide in order to assess your application. The legal bases are Article 6(1)(b) GDPR in
      conjunction with section 26(1) BDSG for carrying out the application procedure, and your consent under
      Article 6(1)(a) GDPR, which you give by taking part voluntarily. Participation is optional; you can also
      apply to us without taking the aptitude test.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google may also process data outside the European Economic Area. Such transfers rely on the adequacy
      decision for the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or on EU Standard Contractual Clauses. We delete your test
      results no later than six months after the application procedure has concluded. Google's information:
      policies.google.com/privacy.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Form abuse protection</h2>
    <p>
      After you actively start using a form, Cloudflare Turnstile from Cloudflare, Inc. is loaded to detect
      automated submissions. It processes technical connection, browser and interaction data. The legal basis
      is our legitimate interest in website security under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. A data processing agreement
      is in place.
    </p>

    <h2>6. External videos and maps</h2>
    <p>
      YouTube videos and Google Maps are not loaded automatically. A connection to Google Ireland Limited is
      made only after you allow the relevant service. The legal bases are your consent under Article 6(1)(a)
      GDPR and section 25(1) TDDDG. Your choice is stored locally in your browser as
      <code>wamocon-consent-youtube</code> or <code>wamocon-consent-google-maps</code> until you use “Reset
      external-content choices” in the footer or clear browser storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      Team videos on the careers page are requested from GitHub, Inc. only when you start playback. Your IP
      address is then technically transmitted to GitHub. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR together with
      the playback expressly requested by you.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Cookies, local storage and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      WAMOCON does not use Google Analytics, advertising trackers or a newsletter on this website. The site
      stores only your voluntary external-content choices locally in the browser. Cloudflare Turnstile may use
      technically necessary storage when you actively use a form.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Recipients and international transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Recipients may include Vercel, Microsoft and, when a form is used, Cloudflare. Google/YouTube is contacted
      only after consent; GitHub is contacted only after an externally hosted video is started. Google Ireland
      Limited also receives data if you voluntarily take the aptitude test via Google Forms. Processing
      outside the EEA relies on an adequacy decision such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or appropriate
      safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Retention and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      We retain personal data only for as long as the purpose or legal retention duties require. You have the
      rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, data portability and objection under the GDPR.
      Consent can be withdrawn at any time for the future. Contact
      <a href="mailto:info@wamocon.com">info@wamocon.com</a> to exercise your rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may lodge a complaint with a data protection authority, in particular the Hessian Commissioner for
      Data Protection and Freedom of Information at
      <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">datenschutz.hessen.de</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Security and updates</h2>
    <p>
      We protect the website with TLS encryption and appropriate technical and organisational measures. This
      policy is updated when functions, processors or legal requirements change.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
